<title>Objects and Obstacles</title>
<style>
:root{--bg:#f4f5f3;--panel:#fff;--ink:#1c2320;--muted:#5e6964;--rule:#d8ddd9;--serif:"Times New Roman",Times,"Nimbus Roman",serif}
@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark){:root:not([data-theme="light"]){color-scheme:dark;--bg:#141816;--panel:#1c211f;--ink:#e4e9e6;--muted:#9aa6a0;--rule:#2e3633}}
:root[data-theme="dark"]{color-scheme:dark;--bg:#141816;--panel:#1c211f;--ink:#e4e9e6;--muted:#9aa6a0;--rule:#2e3633}
body{background:var(--bg);color:var(--ink);font-family:var(--serif);font-size:17px;line-height:1.5}
.wrap{max-width:1300px;margin:0 auto;padding-inline:20px;padding-block:26px 44px;display:grid;gap:24px}
h1{font-size:30px;margin:0;line-height:1.15;text-wrap:balance}.lede{color:var(--muted);max-width:85ch;margin:6px 0 0}
h2{font-size:21px;margin:0}.case{display:grid;gap:12px;background:var(--panel);border:1px solid var(--rule);border-radius:10px;padding:16px}
video,img{width:100%;max-width:100%;border-radius:6px;display:block;background:#fff}figure{margin:0;display:grid;gap:6px}figcaption{font-size:14.5px;color:var(--muted)}
.facts{font-size:15px;color:var(--muted)}.meta{font-size:13px;color:var(--muted);word-break:break-all}
</style>
<div class="wrap">
<header><h1>Pick, carry and place: different objects over different obstacles</h1>
<p class="lede">Each case: the world model plans a pick-and-carry to a target (on the ground, in the air, or on top of furniture) with an obstacle in the way (the obstacle enters the objective as its bounding box with a clearance buffer &mdash; 40 mm for carry-over cases, 3 mm when the object is to rest on it &mdash; weight 5&ndash;10; Adam lr 0.1, 40 iterations, shell on, population 4). The plan's hand trajectory is then executed in Isaac Lab by a controller-driven fixed-base Franka (differential IK into PD joint drives with velocity feedforward, binary gripper), with the obstacle present as an immovable convex-hull collider built from the same asset. Frames are rendered offline from the simulated poses with the objects' own textured meshes (fitted to the frame-0 particles), the obstacle asset, and a dark-green X on the table at the target; the start | end image carries the smoothed path of the object's centroid. Pickup-only checkpoint throughout.</p></header>
<section class="case"><h2>Milk carton placed on top of a wooden cabinet</h2>
<p class="facts">Target = start + (30 cm x, 0, +19.6 cm): the centroid height of the carton standing on the cabinet's top face (libero wooden_cabinet 0170, 19.6 &times; 22.8 &times; 19.6 cm, placed under the target). Planning: 40 iterations, shell on, cabinet box weight 5 with a 3 mm margin (the carton must come to rest on it). Generation: all four members reach the top-face target (3.7 / 3.9 / 13.6 / 11.0 mm). Isaac, commanded arm, cabinet as an immovable collider: member m3 shown &mdash; peak lift 326 mm, carton reaches the cabinet top at frame 54 (video and path cut there); it arrives already tilted 46&deg; and, as the arm keeps moving, ends lying at 71&deg;, 47 mm from the target point (the plan itself ends at 106&deg;); arm tracking 1.7 / 3.7 mm; m1 the same (47 mm). See the upright-term case below. The planner's own pick m0 slipped out of the gripper at lift-off in the arm replay (it succeeds with the floating hand, 37 mm), so this is not the planner-view member.</p>
<div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:14px">
<div><figure><video src="carton_cabinet/arm.mp4" controls autoplay muted loop playsinline preload="auto"></video><figcaption>Rendered carton and cabinet; stops at first contact with the cabinet top (frame 54).</figcaption></figure><figure><img src="carton_cabinet/keyframes.png" alt="Carton on cabinet, rendered: start and end with the centroid path rising over onto the cabinet top"></figure></div>
<div><figure><video src="carton_cabinet/arm_hull.mp4" controls autoplay muted loop playsinline preload="auto"></video><figcaption>Hull &amp; box style.</figcaption></figure><figure><img src="carton_cabinet/keyframes_hull.png" alt="Carton on cabinet, hull style: start and end with the centroid path"></figure></div>
</div></section>
<section class="case"><h2>Milk carton placed on the cabinet, with an upright term</h2>
<p class="facts">Same task and settings as the cabinet case above plus an upright term: the tilt of the carton's frame-0 vertical axis (Kabsch rotation of its particles, differentiable), averaged over the last 5 frames, weighted 0.3 m per radian. Generation, final tilt per member: 84&deg; / 101&deg; / 12&deg; / 106&deg; without the term &rarr; <b>1.9&deg; / 4.1&deg; / 3.5&deg; / 0.7&deg;</b> with it (goal distances 12.5 / 41.8 / 72.3 / 73.6 mm; planner pick m3). Isaac, commanded arm, cabinet collider, member m3: carton reaches the cabinet top at frame 51 (video and path cut there) tilted <b>15&deg;</b>, standing; as the arm keeps pressing after contact it settles at 26&deg; by frame 60, 71 mm from the target point (+199 mm up). Without the term: 46&deg; at contact, 71&deg; at the end. Arm tracking 5.2 / 40 mm, the deviation during that post-contact push (frames 52&ndash;58).</p>
<div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:14px">
<div><figure><video src="carton_cabinet_upright/arm.mp4" controls autoplay muted loop playsinline preload="auto"></video><figcaption>Rendered carton and cabinet, upright term; stops at first contact (frame 51).</figcaption></figure><figure><img src="carton_cabinet_upright/keyframes.png" alt="Carton on cabinet with upright term, rendered: start and end, carton standing on the cabinet"></figure></div>
<div><figure><video src="carton_cabinet_upright/arm_hull.mp4" controls autoplay muted loop playsinline preload="auto"></video><figcaption>Hull &amp; box style.</figcaption></figure><figure><img src="carton_cabinet_upright/keyframes_hull.png" alt="Carton on cabinet with upright term, hull style: start and end"></figure></div>
</div></section>
<section class="case"><h2>Milk carton placed on a cabinet standing to the side</h2>
<p class="facts">Same cabinet and upright term, but the cabinet stands 30 cm to the carton's side (+y): target = start + (0, 30 cm, +19.6 cm). Generation: 57 / 61 / 11 / 160 mm; planner pick m2. Isaac, commanded arm, cabinet collider: carton carried sideways and set on the cabinet top (+191 mm), <b>7.9&deg; tilt at first contact</b> (frame 57, where the video and path stop); as the arm keeps executing it settles at 40&deg; and 116 mm from the target point by frame 60. Arm tracking 4.3 / 45 mm (the deviation at set-down). Camera from the far side of the robot, looking back at it, so the arm partly covers the carton mid-carry.</p>
<div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:14px">
<div><figure><video src="carton_cabinet_side/arm.mp4" controls autoplay muted loop playsinline preload="auto"></video><figcaption>Rendered; stops at first contact.</figcaption></figure><figure><img src="carton_cabinet_side/keyframes.png" alt="Carton placed on a cabinet to the side, rendered: start and contact frame with the sideways path"></figure></div>
<div><figure><video src="carton_cabinet_side/arm_hull.mp4" controls autoplay muted loop playsinline preload="auto"></video><figcaption>Hull &amp; box style.</figcaption></figure><figure><img src="carton_cabinet_side/keyframes_hull.png" alt="Carton placed on a cabinet to the side, hull style"></figure></div>
</div></section>
<section class="case"><h2>Milk carton over a row of stacked books</h2>
<p class="facts">Obstacle: three stacks of three books lying flat (libero book 0004 &times; 9, each offset and yawed a little), 39.7 cm long, 14.9 cm deep, 10.6 cm high, midway. Target = start + (30 cm x, +4 cm y) on the ground. Planning: 40 iterations, shell on, book-row box weight 10 with a 40 mm buffer. Generation: 41 / 33 / 324 / 60 mm; planner pick m1 (33 mm), whose closest approach to the box in the plan is 41 mm. Isaac, commanded arm, nine book hulls as immovable colliders: carton carried over (peak 233 mm), set down 45 mm from the target, resting 28 mm above its start height against the landing; arm tracking 4.3 / 47 mm (the deviation is at the set-down, frames 52&ndash;55). Floating hand on the same member: 43 mm.</p>
<div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:14px">
<div><figure><video src="carton_books/arm.mp4" controls autoplay muted loop playsinline preload="auto"></video><figcaption>Rendered carton and books.</figcaption></figure><figure><img src="carton_books/keyframes.png" alt="Carton over books, rendered: start and end with the centroid path arcing over the book row"></figure></div>
<div><figure><video src="carton_books/arm_hull.mp4" controls autoplay muted loop playsinline preload="auto"></video><figcaption>Hull &amp; box style.</figcaption></figure><figure><img src="carton_books/keyframes_hull.png" alt="Carton over books, hull style: start and end with the centroid path"></figure></div>
</div></section>
<section class="case"><h2>Cases whose grasp did not hold in the simulator</h2>
<p class="facts">Plans that reach their target in generation but whose pick does not transfer to Isaac. Shown as rendered; each with its numbers.</p>
<div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr 1fr;gap:14px">
<div><h3 style="margin:0 0 6px;font-size:16px">Peanut butter jar over the row of books, air target</h3><figure><video src="jar_books/arm.mp4" controls muted loop playsinline preload="metadata"></video></figure><figure><img src="jar_books/keyframes.png" alt="Jar over books: the grasp slips at lift-off"><figcaption>Target 30 cm away, 15 cm up; generation 2 mm (pick m3). Isaac: the grasp slips at lift-off (27 mm peak; floating hand 23 mm); afterwards the empty arm is briefly blocked by the book row on its way down (hand error up to 248 mm, frames 45&ndash;50).</figcaption></figure></div>
<div><h3 style="margin:0 0 6px;font-size:16px">Pasta box over the row of books</h3><figure><video src="pastabox_books/arm.mp4" controls muted loop playsinline preload="metadata"></video></figure><figure><img src="pastabox_books/keyframes.png" alt="Pasta box over books: dropped in mid-air"><figcaption>Cramped setup: the 14.7 cm box starts 15 cm from a 15 cm-deep row with a 4 cm buffer, so the obstacle term never clears (29&ndash;58 mm intrusion at iteration 40). Generation 71 mm (pick m0); Isaac: lifted to 93 mm, then the grasp slips at frame ~40 and the box falls beside the books (floating hand carried it to 90 mm).</figcaption></figure></div>
<div><h3 style="margin:0 0 6px;font-size:16px">Soda can over the row of books</h3><figure><video src="can_books/arm.mp4" controls muted loop playsinline preload="metadata"></video></figure><figure><img src="can_books/keyframes.png" alt="Soda can over books: the can is knocked over at the grasp"><figcaption>Generation 35 mm from the target (pick m0); Isaac: the gripper closes on the can at frame 20 and leaves without it; can knocked over (floating hand the same, 9 mm peak lift).</figcaption></figure></div>
<div><h3 style="margin:0 0 6px;font-size:16px">Water bottle over a basket, air target</h3><figure><video src="bottle_basket/arm.mp4" controls muted loop playsinline preload="metadata"></video></figure><figure><img src="bottle_basket/keyframes.png" alt="Water bottle over basket: bottle never lifted"><figcaption>Target 30 cm away and 10 cm up; generation 22 mm (pick m0); Isaac: bottle never lifted (0&ndash;4 mm peak, all four members, floating hand and arm).</figcaption></figure></div>
<div><h3 style="margin:0 0 6px;font-size:16px">Pasta box over a caddy (ill-posed)</h3><figure><video src="pastabox_caddy/arm.mp4" controls muted loop playsinline preload="metadata"></video></figure><figure><img src="pastabox_caddy/keyframes.png" alt="Pasta box over caddy: not lifted"><figcaption>The caddy is 19.7 cm deep; with the 40 mm buffer its exclusion zone already contains the box's start position (obstacle term 105&ndash;115 mm before any guidance), so a 30 cm carry cannot satisfy the objective. Isaac: not lifted.</figcaption></figure></div>
</div></section>
<section class="case"><h2>Peanut butter jar over a tea box (pipeline check; the plan itself failed)</h2><p class="facts">target +25 cm x on the ground; obstacle tea_box 0001 (6.6 &times; 7.1 &times; 12.0 cm). Generation: best member ends 197 mm from the target (all four 197&ndash;211 mm; unguided 416&ndash;491). Isaac (commanded arm): the jar is never lifted (peak 10 mm), gets knocked over and ends 26 mm below its start height; arm tracking 1.0 / 2.4 mm. Shown for the rendering pipeline: real jar and tea-box meshes, tea box as a physical obstacle.</p>
<figure><video src="jar_teabox/arm.mp4" controls autoplay muted loop playsinline preload="auto"></video><figcaption>61 frames at 20 fps.</figcaption></figure>
<figure><img src="jar_teabox/keyframes.png" alt="Peanut butter jar over a tea box (pipeline check; the plan itself failed): frame 0 and frame 60 with the object's centroid path"><figcaption>Frame 0 (left) and frame 60 (right) with the smoothed centroid path.</figcaption></figure></section>

<p class="meta">runs/pickup/obst_*/ (result.json, rollout.npz, replay_isaac/, replay_isaac_arm/{isaac,render_asset,render_x}) &middot; bin/replay_arm.py --obstacle_asset --auto_camera &middot; pickup_replay_isaac/scripts/replay_isaac_arm.py --obstacle_mesh, render_arm_replay.py --obstacle_mesh</p>
</div>
